      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Holding onto something tangible like your sword, even through the pain, indicates a flicker of enduring purpose, however grim. That weight of reality you feel is a signal that even in ruin, a core part of you remains active. Instead of viewing it as a tomb, could you see this moment as a final, terrible chapter where you are the most powerful survivor left? Focus not on rebuilding the kingdom, but on the weight of your own will to simply *remain* for one more hour.",
